  "summary": "The European Affairs Committee questioned Lord Wood of Anfield and Paul Hughes from the Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office about the new UK-EU treaty on Gibraltar. The agreement aims to keep the land border with Spain flowing smoothly, protect British sovereignty over Gibraltar, and give Gibraltar and the surrounding region economic stability. The witnesses explained why the deal took five years, how it affects military personnel and customs, and how disputes and termination would work. They also faced tough questions about Spanish powers, sovereignty, and the treaty’s exit clauses.",
